ing saved  unable to keep the tense community  afloat don resorts to more hostile  measures basically enslaving anyone that  the police find  in a world where humanity is scarce and  decisions are being made on a life or  death level  having to defer to the judgment and  power of a former law enforcement  officer  just sounds like a nightmare for dawn  and her citizens  life becomes about serving a singular  goal keeping her  in power that seems like a great deal  for dawn less so for everyone else  woodbury gets credit for being one of  the first safe havens built from the  ground up  after the onset of the apocalypse early  on in the show's timeline  the governor leads a small group of  people to clear out fortify  and make the town somewhat  self-sustaining at a time when most  other people were wandering the woods  under the governor's leadership they  even managed to plant crops and get the  power back on so that some small slice  of normal life was restored to a little  more than 70 people  however although comfortable the  residents of woodbury are completely  unaware of the day-to-day danger they  face  mostly from their insane leader i'm  sorry it's just this place is  [Music]  i can't stay here why the governor he is  not what he seems to  be the viewers know the governor to be a  heinous individual capable of horrific  crimes  however the average person who sees  tomatoes growing in their neighborhood  probably isn't looking too closely at  where the latest shipment of supplies  came from  this ignorance comes to a head during  the war with rick grimes's group in the  prison  the citizens of woodbury think  themselves the good guys when they  launch their attack but some of the  survivors of the battle are cut down by  the governor himself  not exactly a community where you can  depend on your leader  once you survive the apocalypse the  question becomes what kind of day-to-day  life is acceptable for you to survive in  for the members of the scavengers t