nd its citizens dwindle  while the community gets credit for  changing with the times the fact is that  ezekiel invests  long term in a place with a short  expiration date  the prison may seem like a great place  to live and rick and his group of  survivors do their best to make it one  for a long time  however the logistics of maintaining a  prison are a constant struggle  for one the place was designed to be  maintained by a large staff of guards  cooks administrators and more when in  doubt  prison labor filled in the gaps when the  survivors arrive  it's up to a little more than a dozen  people to manage a massive facility  while blocking off a section of the  prison is easy enough they are  constantly plagued by walkers getting  past the gate  meanwhile its curbside appeal makes it a  constant target for attacks which is  ultimately how the prison  falls in a desperate world having  something as shiny and secure as a  prison  is too often an invitation for outsiders  to take what isn't theirs  a place can be as safe as possible from  walkers but as the show constantly  reminds its audience  human beings are the real threat in this  world  the community of oceanside is created  after another settlement falls to the  ruthless tactics of the savior simon  after suffering a defeat that sees every  male member of their society executed  the women and children flee to  re-establish themselves elsewhere  they become the first group on this list  to utilize their natural geography  by putting the ocean at their back to  prevent walkers coming at them from  every side  they decide that sharing what they have  with the world is no longer an  option because someone like simon will  eventually strong-arm their way into  taking it  as a result they spend most of their  time doing the bare minimum to survive  while getting rid of anyone that might  make their presence known to the rest of  the world  unfortunately their main concern is  staying hidden which prevents them from  really building the oceanside community  into something grand  until after rick's war with negan even  then  resources are scarce and oceanside  becomes little more than a stopping  point for people to travel to more  secure locations  however the community gets a lot of  credit for being naturally fortified  from the water as well as standing tall  in the face of defeat  oceanside also gets top marks for its  resilience and tactical position  fortified walls an endless supply of  fighters resources  and a somewhat merit-based economy if  that sounds like a good time  the sanctuary might be up your alley of  course it's not all sunshine and  lollipops members of the sanctuary are  asked to join an incredibly unforgiving  cult that promises safety in exchange  for entering a debt system  similar to that of grady memorial  hospital if you decide that you're not  happy with the deal  you can always run however negan and the  saviors are powerful enough to collect  on their debts  unfortunately all it takes is a run-in  with rick grimes for everything to  crumble  the problem with ruling by fear is that  once you encounter someone that isn't  afraid to take a few hits you can't just  take your ball and go home  negan understands that which is why he  wages total war on rick and his alliance  of communities  he knows that there is no way to  continue ruling by force if there is an  equally powerful civilization in the  area with a more enlightened view on  corporal punishment  similar to the sanctuary terminus is a  large brick facility that is easily  fortified and manned by people to ensure  the dead state out  its people don't even need to risk  venturing out into the world for  supplies  everything they need in terms of weapons  equipment and yes food  is delivered right to their front door  after resorting to cannibalism following  a horrific attack  leader gareth advertises terminus as a  safe haven for survivors  that's just the sales pitch however  anyone who 