ce and if they did  they'd have large walls and guards with  weapons to contend with  the community is even self-sustaining  with fertile ground and dependable crops  without the need to venture outside  however the true strength of the hilltop  is in its leadership  for all his flaws gregory was the exact  person hilltop needed to establish and  secure the safe haven  however when he proves ineffective as a  wartime leader the people are lucky  enough to see maggie take charge  when all else is failing around them the  hilltop digs in and manages to survive  while other more seemingly secure and  stock communities  fall like dominoes not only is it a  well-built place to live  but it's led by people who are just  hardened enough to keep it safe without  resorting to drastic measures  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite television shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

