m  really building the oceanside community  into something grand  until after rick's war with negan even  then  resources are scarce and oceanside  becomes little more than a stopping  point for people to travel to more  secure locations  however the community gets a lot of  credit for being naturally fortified  from the water as well as standing tall  in the face of defeat  oceanside also gets top marks for its  resilience and tactical position  fortified walls an endless supply of  fighters resources  and a somewhat merit-based economy if  that sounds like a good time  the sanctuary might be up your alley of  course it's not all sunshine and  lollipops members of the sanctuary are  asked to join an incredibly unforgiving  cult that promises safety in exchange  for entering a debt system  similar to that of grady memorial  hospital if you decide that you're not  happy with the deal  you can always run however negan and the  saviors are powerful enough to collect  on their debts  unfortunately all it takes is a run-in  with rick grimes for everything to  crumble  the problem with ruling by fear is that  once you encounter someone that isn't  afraid to take a few hits you can't just  take your ball and go home  negan understands that which is why he  wages total war on rick and his alliance  of communities  he knows that there is no way to  continue ruling by force if there is an  equally powerful civilization in the  area with a more enlightened view on  corporal punishment  similar to the sanctuary terminus is a  large brick facility that is easily  fortified and manned by people to ensure  the dead state out  its people don't even need to risk  venturing out into the world for  supplies  everything they need in terms of weapons  equipment and yes food  is delivered right to their front door  after resorting to cannibalism following  a horrific attack  leader gareth advertises terminus as a  safe haven for survivors  that's just the sales pitch however  anyone who makes it to terminus has to  give up their gear before getting made  into a feast for real terminus residents  gareth builds a society that is  sustainable and secure  however the cost of entry is becoming a  straight up cannibal  one can only survive so long on morally  questionable societal means  but gareth manages to make it last for a  surprisingly long time  this safe haven has literally everything  alexandria is a community that was  converted from an upscale suburban  neighborhood  originally designed for sustainability  once the apocalypse hits  a professor of architecture redesigns  and fortifies the walls to ensure that  both  people and walkers can't get in there's  enough space in empty houses for people  to really set down some roots knowing  that they don't have to worry about the  wasteland outside  plus its location near a mall means  years of guaranteed supplies before  needing to look elsewhere  in short alexandria ticks off all the  boxes of both safety and comfort  however being comfortable and safe isn't  always the best thing for people in an  apocalypse  similar to the prison when you have  something that looks this great to a  desperate outsider  it will forever be a target since  settling down in alexandria its citizens  have done nothing but fight the outside  world to varying degrees of success  still if you like a lot of danger and  excitement in your life  alexandria might be the place for you it  may not be the flashiest  it may not be the most comfortable but  it's definitely survived and thrived  more than any other community with more  potential the hilltop starts out as a  historic museum house in virginia before  the apocalypse turns it into a safe zone  when the military abandons it the  survivors decide it's the perfect place  to build a stronghold  its location in the wilderness means  that large invasions by walkers aren't  likely  and easy to see coming if the impossible  does occur survivors can't really sneak  up on the place and if they did  they'd have large walls and guards with  weapons to contend with  the community is even self-sustaining  with fertile ground and dependable crops  without the need to venture outside  however the true strength of the hilltop  is in its leadership  for all his flaws gregory was the exact  person hilltop needed to establish and  secure the safe haven  however when he proves ineffective as a  wartime leader the people are lucky  enough to see maggie take charge  when all else is failing around them the  hilltop digs in and manages to survive  while other more seemingly secure and  stock communities  fall like dominoes not only is it a  well-built place to live  but it's led by people who are just  hardened enough to keep it safe without  resorting to drastic measures  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite television shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one


